fix(controller): trim trailing whitespace from the prompt

BPE word tokens carry their leading space (" the"), so a prompt ending
in " " — which every trigger keystroke produces — starves all real word
tokens and surfaces the junk that follows a space without one: bare
numbers, <strong>/<em> tags, quotes. Trim trailing whitespace before
sending; returned tokens then carry the space themselves and firstWord
already strips it. Deepening re-joins prompt + " " + candidate to keep
the boundary clean. Probe script normalizes identically. Verified live:
"Paris is " now yields a/the/one/known/not instead of 10/2017/<strong>.

